b &= 6c - 3 \\
\end{align*}
The third equation gives us $a = 3b + c$. We can substitute $b = 6c - 3$ into this equation to get $a = 3(6c - 3) + c$.
\begin{align*}
a &= 3(6c - 3) + c \\
a &= 18c - 9 + c \\
a &= 19c - 9 \\
